# Frontend conventions

- Astro stays in `output: "static"` mode. Every route is a prerendered
  physical file except exactly one: `apps/site/src/pages/api/ask.ts`, which
  sets `prerender = false` and runs through a Vercel adapter. No other route
  becomes dynamic without a superseding ADR.
- Preact hydrates at most two islands: an interactive map and the Ask Diego
  guide. Every other route ships no client framework JavaScript.
- Never import server-only Ask-Diego code, runtime configuration, or a
  secret name into browser-reachable code.
- Every route required in English has a Spanish counterpart at its `/es/`
  path with essential-content parity; do not ship one language ahead of the
  other for a required route.
- Keep and measure a first-party JavaScript budget per route. Motion is
  non-essential decoration and must fully respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- Factual portfolio text renders from typed content/manifest sources, not
  copied prose in component files; project status badges render only from a
  validated manifest field, never a hardcoded label.
- Use semantic HTML, native controls, skip links, visible focus, and
  keyboard-complete interaction for both Preact islands.
- No prohibited anti-slop pattern from `DESIGN.md` (or the eventual
  visual-direction ADR) appears — no fake terminal, no fabricated dashboard
  metrics, no AI-generated portrait.
